  "text_pages": [
    "Home - International Welcome e-desk - University of Strasbourg\nInternational Students of the University of Strasbourg: We're Here to Help!\nWelcome to the University of Strasbourg\nInternational students and PhD students, teacher-researchers, you will find here all the information and contacts you need to prepare your visit, organize your stay and discover your new living environment.\nBetter understand your\nstudent profile\nBetter understand your\nresearcher profile\nBefore\nmy arrival\nI am\nin\nStrasbourg\nBefore\nmy departure\nOur Events\nCap sur l'international | European Parliament guided visit\nConcerned profiles :\nInternational\nAs part of “Cap sur l’international”, the University of Strasbourg invites you to discover one of Strasbourg’s iconic…\n16/10/2026\n13:45\n/\n15:30\nEuropean Parliament\nAll events\nA simple registration in our catalog grants you access to a multitude of dedicated services.\nA simple registration in our catalog grants you access to a multitude of dedicated services.\nDepending on your profile (student or researcher) and your needs, the University of Strasbourg assists you throughout your stay in France.\nOn this platform, the University of Strasbourg offers regular activities.\nRegister in just a few clicks to benefit from or share these services with those around you.\nHere are some examples of services offered by the University of Strasbourg\nAdministrative Support\nHelp with social security registration, tax returns, visas... Find your way around the French administration.\nCultural Outings\nFind out more about the University, the city of Strasbourg and all its cultural attractions.\nEvents\nKeep informed about events at the University of Strasbourg, and the most important times in Strasbourg's life.\nLearning French (FLE)\nWe offer to international students and researchers classes to learn or improve their French.\nServices Pack catalog\nWelcome\nExplore the libraries' collection of objects\n23/09/2026\nUniversity libraries are breaking new ground and now offer students the chance to borrow everyday items!\nResearch\nPodcast | Materials of the Future: Gold, Light, and CO₂\n21/09/2026\nPodcast | “Science Challenges, Society Challenges” Season 2, Episode 1. Can we draw inspiration from plants to turn carbon dioxide into a resource? How can light help us generate energy while…\nInternational\nBuddy programme | Wine & Cheese tasting event\n20/04/2026\nOn April 16th, the Maison Universitaire Internationale hosted a typically French event : Wine & Cheese tasting.\nInternational\nRomanian Ambassador Visits the University of Strasbourg\n26/03/2026\nOn March 19, the University of Strasbourg welcomed Ms. Ioana Bivolaru, Romanian Ambassador to France, accompanied by Mr. Vierita, Romanian Consul in Strasbourg.\nAll the news\nHazan : International student et the University of Strasbourg\nCulture\n15/04/2026\n\"I feel free, my perspective has been widened in a lot of aspects with learning new cultures\"\nAll testimonies\nMenu\nBrowse those links to navigate the website\nDisplay\nHide\nthe searchbox\nFill in your search :\nLaunch search\nClose\nOur audiences :\nStudent Profile\nResearcher Profile\nI think about it\nBefore\nmy arrival\nI am\nin\nStrasbourg\nBefore\nmy departure\nServices Pack"
  ],
